      <Desc>IMPROVE AND ASSIST THE EDUCATIONAL SYSTEM AND STUDENTS OF THE EDUCATIONAL SYSTEM OF THE STATE OF CALIFORNIA; PROMOTE EDUCATIONAL GOALS.The CATE Convention was held in Burlingame on Feb 28 - March 2. Attendance was 765. Speakers included Tina Korani, Gerry Brooks, CUE, CAP CUE, Dashka Slater. The theme was Social Context Using Pop Culture and Social Media to Make Content Relevant. We included Educator Meetup to share strategies to help all thrive in what can be challenging environmentsWe developed and adopted resolutions on the following topics. We continue to work on Active Mission Statement Work (Franks Amiesh activity)Discussing and sessions addressed AI in Education.Officers and Local Affiliates attended NCTEs annual convention in Boston in November, we received an award to increase membership and attended required business meetings and get-togethers. We had four board meetings in Sept, Dec, Feb and May. Committee Chairs for 2025-2026: Leadership/Membership Joan Williams; Convention Coordinating Chair Jennifer Silver; Policy/Censorship April Parker; Executive Finance Susan Dillon; Publications/Social Media Carole LeCren.We published 4 issues of California English - due to law changes in California, the Precision Assembly can no longer manage our mailing list and send out our publications. We located another vendor Sundance Press who is able to take over the job. California English received NCTE Award for Excellence in Journals at their annual convention in Boston</Desc>
